# The section that was /games/ is /apps/. Most of what lives there is not a game — the typing
# trainer, the guitar flashcards, the tuner, the sleep log — and the ones that are lose nothing by
# sitting under a heading that no longer claims to describe them.
#
# 301 rather than 302 because the old routes are not coming back. Note what this does to an
# already-installed home-screen app: its start_url redirects out of its own scope, so iOS opens
# the target in Safari instead of the app. That is what renaming a PWA's routes means, and the
# fix is deleting the old icon and installing the new one once.
#
# The old fretboard/transpose routes are listed before the catch-all, because first match wins
# and /games/fretboard must reach the flashcards rather than a /apps/fretboard that does not
# exist. The stats tabs land on their own halves rather than on the practice screen: someone
# with /games/fretboard/stats bookmarked wants a progress page, and the neck heatmap is still
# one. See the "Flashcards" section of CLAUDE.md.

# www -> apex is NOT here, and cannot be: Cloudflare rejects a deploy whose _redirects source is
# absolute ("Line N: Only relative URLs are allowed"), so this file cannot match on hostname the
# way _headers can. It is a zone Single Redirect instead - the one piece of the serving path that
# is not in this repo. See "The zone's records" in CLAUDE.md.

/games/fretboard              /apps/flashcards           301
/games/fretboard/stats        /apps/flashcards/neck      301
/games/transpose              /apps/flashcards           301
/games/transpose/stats        /apps/flashcards/chords    301

/pl/games/fretboard           /pl/apps/flashcards        301
/pl/games/fretboard/stats     /pl/apps/flashcards/neck   301
/pl/games/transpose           /pl/apps/flashcards        301
/pl/games/transpose/stats     /pl/apps/flashcards/chords 301

/apps/fretboard               /apps/flashcards           301
/apps/fretboard/stats         /apps/flashcards/neck      301
/apps/transpose               /apps/flashcards           301
/apps/transpose/stats         /apps/flashcards/chords    301

/pl/apps/fretboard            /pl/apps/flashcards        301
/pl/apps/fretboard/stats      /pl/apps/flashcards/neck   301
/pl/apps/transpose            /pl/apps/flashcards        301
/pl/apps/transpose/stats      /pl/apps/flashcards/chords 301

# The bedtime checklist was briefly its own app before it became a tab of the sleep log, which
# is where it belonged: it is read at the same hour and by the same person.
/apps/night-routine           /apps/baby-sleep/checklist    301
/pl/apps/night-routine        /pl/apps/baby-sleep/checklist 301

# Event Watch's Pipeline tab is gone (Sep 2026). It listed the whole corpus with eight facets over
# it; what it was actually opened for — has a model read these rows, and what are the filters doing
# to them — is now drawn under each source on the Sources tab, which is where the judgement is made.
# Both the bare and the slashed form, because this is a route an installed app precached.
/apps/events/pipeline         /apps/events/sources          301
/apps/events/pipeline/*       /apps/events/sources          301
/pl/apps/events/pipeline      /pl/apps/events/sources       301
/pl/apps/events/pipeline/*    /pl/apps/events/sources       301

# And the Interests tab is gone too (Sep 2026). The feed is now what the enabled sources collected,
# so the question "what am I watching for?" is answered per source — which is where the Sources tab
# already answered "and how would I know if that were wrong". Same shape of rule as the Pipeline
# one above, and for the same reason: this is a route an installed app precached.
/apps/events/interests        /apps/events/sources          301
/apps/events/interests/*      /apps/events/sources          301
/pl/apps/events/interests     /pl/apps/events/sources       301
/pl/apps/events/interests/*   /pl/apps/events/sources       301

# The admissions panel was /admin/ for one morning, before it became an app — which is the only
# place anything here is actually found. The old path is in one deploy's worth of bookmarks and
# in the link the login page shipped with, so it keeps working.
/admin                        /apps/admin                301
/pl/admin                     /pl/apps/admin             301

/games/*                      /apps/:splat               301
/pl/games/*                   /pl/apps/:splat            301
